<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Jan-Sept oil products demand up 7.2 pct.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Jan-Sept oil products demand up 7.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's oil products demand grew 7.2 percent to 517.5 million barrels in the first nine months of 1996 from 482.9 million a year ago, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>This compares with a 9.2 percent rise in domestic consumption in the same period of last year.</p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement the oil refiners produced 520.1 million barrels of petroleum products in the first nine months against 474.1 million a year before.</p>
<p>Hyundai Oil Refinery Co's new 200,000 barrels-per-day (bpd) crude distillation unit, which started operation in late February, boosted the output.</p>
<p>South Korea currently has a refining capacity of 2.22 million bpd.  </p>
<p>Oil products demand (in million barrels)</p>
<p>				    Jan-Sept	 Jan-Sept 1995</p>
<p>    TOTAL			  517.5	    482.9</p>
<p>MAJOR PRODUCTS</p>
<p>     gasoline		     50.2	     43.6</p>
<p>     kerosene		     45.1	     39.0</p>
<p>     diesel			125.8	    115.2</p>
<p>     C-type fuel oil	   119.0	    118.6</p>
<p>     naphtha		     104.1	     96.7</p>
<p>     LPG			    49.2	     47.6</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
